<title>HONG KONG: Dah Sing Financial 1996 net up 26.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Dah Sing Financial 1996 net up 26.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   264.0     vs 209.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    62.0	vs 52.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  6.70 gain vs 17.76 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    602.61    vs 476.55</p>
<p>    Company name		 Dah Sing Financial Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  April 14-18</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   April 29</p>
<p>NOTE - Dah Sing provides banking and related financial services.</p>
<p>The company proposes a special dividend of HK$0.10 per share.</p>
<p>The exceptional items represents the profit on disposal of fixed assets and long-term investments.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 113 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 41 cents and special dividend) vs 85 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
